# Input through SDL's own loop: typed text into a's number box, keys, Tab, a trackpad pinch and a
# wheel with Ctrl held, and the system's appearance flipped (on macOS through NSApp's appearance,
# which SDL observes as it observes the system's). --trace logs each fact as the app reads it.
# a's box is (330, 408.5, 107, 32) at 1440 x 900; the plane right of x 488, its empty
# background at (700, 700) (tools/src/loop.py's PLANE: no mark there to take hold of).
size 1440 900
density 2
wait 1000
click 383 424
wait 100
type "1.5"
key Backspace
type "25"
wait 300
shot typed
wait 600
key Enter            # the field closes and the box keeps the focus
tab                  # k's box
tab                  # b's flip toggle
tab                  # b's box
tab shift            # b's flip toggle again
tab                  # b's box
key Enter            # b's field opens
wait 900
move 700 700
pinch 1.25
wheel 0 -50 ctrl
wait 300
scheme light
wait 400
scheme dark
wait 400
shot end
wait 600
